      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:4:6:6",
      "text": [
        " رُفِعَ إِلَى أَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ( عليه السلام ) سِتَّةُ غِلْمَانٍ كَانُوا فِي الْفُرَاتِ فَغَرِقَ وَاحِدٌ مِنْهُمْ فَشَهِدَ ثَلَاثَةٌ مِنْهُمْ عَلَى اثْنَيْنِ أَنَّهُمَا غَرَّقَاهُ وَ شَهِدَ اثْنَانِ عَلَى الثَّلَاثَةِ أَنَّهُمْ غَرَّقُوهُ فَقَضَى ( عليه السلام ) بِالدِّيَةِ أَخْمَاساً ثَلَاثَةَ أَخْمَاسٍ عَلَى الِاثْنَيْنِ وَ خُمُسَيْنِ عَلَى الثَّلَاثَةِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Al Nowfaly, from Al Sakuny, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘It was raised to Amir Al-Momineen<sup>asws</sup>, six boys were in the Euphrates, so one of them drowned. So three from them testified against the two that these two drowned him, and the two testified against the three that they drowned him. So he<sup>asws</sup> judged with the wergild be five (parts), three-fifths be upon the two, and two-fifths be upon the three’."
        ]
      }
    },
